@0    = ~Sometimes it feels like travelling with <CHARNAME> is a long way away from home.~
@1    = ~Well, it's a ways from Beregost down here, isn't it?~
@2    = ~That's not what I mean. The adventuring I used to do before - at the time it seemed like we did such amazing things, and now I look back and wonder at how naive I was.~
@3    = ~Not naive. Sensible. If you weren't amazed at what you did, you might've gotten over your head. Best to keep level-headed, and then accidents won't happen.~
@4    = ~Yes! They'd do that exact same thing. "Come here, Auren, you've got homework to do".~
@5    = ~Must be a parent thing. "Come and help me do the accounts, Faren, you're obviously at a loose end".~
@6    = ~"If you insist on playing with swords all day, at least do the dishes in the evening!"~
@7    = ~"Stop messing around with those frogs!"~
@8    = ~Uh, what?~
@9    = ~Oh - that must've just been me, then...~
@10   = ~I understand you worked with some...unsavoury characters in the past. I guess that's a risk when you're in our profession - you can end up in sticky situations.~
@11   = ~Oh, gods, yes.~
@12   = ~When did you know when to draw the line? When your mercenary work became something worse?~
@13   = ~There was a woman in some small town called Lila, and she was crazy. I mean, really crazy. She bottled a woman in the eye for looking at her funny.~
@14   = ~Anyway, she hired me to kill this woman Amy for her. Said she'd stolen a pack of Black Lotus, or some such. At that point, I was almost ready to go with it.~
@15   = ~So then what happened? I hope you didn't do it!~
@16   = ~I'd like to say I had some big epiphany, but really, I drank so much to steel myself up for it that I passed out. When I woke up, someone had stolen all my gold.~
@17   = ~That was when I decided enough was enough and I'd head back to Trademeet.~
@18   = ~Well, it would have been nice to hear a more...heroic story, but thank you for telling me all the same.~
